: NeuralNote wire-contract fixture C6 — a REAL OpenRouter streamed tool-call turn.
:
: Captured 2026-08-10 from https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions with
: stream=true and tools advertised. Model z-ai/glm-5.2 via provider Venice. These
: are the provider's bytes, unedited: no frame here was written by hand, and no
: field inside a frame has been altered. This file is the single source of truth
: for the streamed tool-call shape — a test that hand-writes its own idea of a
: tool-call frame is testing its author's mental model, not the wire.
:
: WHAT THE FULL CAPTURE CONTAINED (3461 data frames, 1.2 MB)
:   - 3425 tool_call entries, every one carrying `index` (values 0-15).
:   - 16 tool calls: 1 search_notes and 15 duplicate write_notes. The runaway is
:     not hypothetical — it is what the very first capture did.
:   - `id` and `function.name` each sent EXACTLY ONCE per call, on first sight.
:   - Arguments arriving as many tiny fragments (386 of them for 4840 chars on
:     index 1; mean 12.5 chars, max 39, min 0).
:   - The stream ending `finish_reason: "error"` with index 15 truncated
:     mid-sentence: 1367 chars that never became valid JSON.
:   - NO \uXXXX escapes anywhere, and no fragment splitting a multi-byte
:     character. Non-ASCII (cafe/e-acute, em dash) arrived as raw UTF-8. Treat
:     that as an UNPROVEN NEGATIVE from one sample, not a guarantee.
:
: WHAT WAS KEPT HERE, AND WHY (701 frames, 238 KB)
:   - 4 leading reasoning frames. A tool stream also carries reasoning and
:     content frames; the accumulator must step over them.
:   - index 0 (search_notes) in full: a small complete call, 4 fragments.
:   - index 1 (write_note) in full: the complete call with the large `content`
:     argument. 386 fragments, boundaries falling inside the JSON string.
:   - index 2 (write_note) in full: the DUPLICATE of index 1 — same body, its
:     own id. Two complete calls that must not bleed into one another, and the
:     raw material for the interleaving corpus.
:   - the first-sight frame ONLY for indices 3-14. Their identity is real; their
:     4840-char argument streams were dropped (13 x 78 KB of the same note).
:   - index 15 (write_note) in full: the call the stream cut off mid-arguments.
:     63 fragments, 1367 chars, never valid JSON. This is the NoteEditAbandoned
:     path, and the capture says it is the COMMON path, not an edge case.
:   - both terminal finish_reason "error" frames, and [DONE].
:
: DO NOT "CLEAN UP" THE EMPTY ARGUMENT FRAGMENTS. `"arguments": ""` appears 32
: times in the full capture and is preserved here. An accumulator that treats an
: empty fragment as a terminator breaks on real traffic, and these frames are the
: only thing that catches it.
:
: Lines beginning with ':' are SSE comments. The live provider sends them too
: (': OPENROUTER PROCESSING'), so a parser that chokes on this header would have
: choked on the real stream.

